{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1787116693,"nonce":"+6eSyX/J1fRIMLYJ9Rexwj7Ao7I=","title":"A snoozed card still offers `Snooze`: §B.8.6's `:bell: Unsnooze` swap never landed, so the action row contradicts the field above it","was":"**What is wrong.** SPEC §B.8.6 specifies that while an alert is snoozed the Slack card's `Snooze` action flips to `:bell: Unsnooze`, and the §H.4 call-out at `docs/design/SPEC.md:3936-3940` repeats it in the same breath as the colour rule: *\"It gains one field — `*Notifications*\\n:zzz: Snoozed by \u003c@U…\u003e until \u003c!date^…\u003e` — and the `Snooze` action flips to `:bell: Unsnooze`.\"* The field landed in `77886a8`. The action swap did not: the card offers `Snooze` to an operator looking at an alert that is already snoozed."}]}